  description: 
  title: Conditional Jumps
  content: 'Lesson 4: Conditional Jumps

    Objective: Introduce the concept of
    jumps and basic program flow control.


    Instructions Covered:

    JZ (Jump
    if Zero): Jump to a specified label if the zero flag is set.

    JNZ (Jump if
    Not Zero): Jump to a label if the zero flag is not set.

    MOV CX, 5

    DEC
    CX

    JNZ LOOP       ; Jump back to LOOP label if CX is not zero

    Exercise
    Application: Use these in Exercise 7 (Jump Jackal) to create a loop that counts
    down.


'
